      "source": [
        "## 2. Create the Features and Target Variable"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b1fjrNpHaoIA"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, we create the variables our classifiers will use. Our target variable (Y) is the **direction of momentum's return next month**: \"Up\" if the return is positive and \"Down\" otherwise. Our 13 features (X) are **this month's returns on all 13 factors**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Unlike our KNN model, which used each factor's own history, this model uses the whole set of factors. The idea is that how all the factors are behaving this month may tell us something about whether momentum will work next month.\n",
        "\n",
        "To do this, we first reshape the data so that each factor has its own column. We keep only months where all 13 factors have data. Debt issuance is the last factor to start (November 1951), so our sample begins there."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "NRejNJPQbOSt"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# reshape the data so each factor has its own column\n",
        "w <- reshape(df0[, c(\"name\", \"date\", \"ret\")], idvar = \"date\",\n",
        "             timevar = \"name\", direction = \"wide\")\n",
        "names(w) <- sub(\"ret.\", \"\", names(w))\n",
        "\n",
        "# sort by date and keep only months where all 13 factors have data\n",
        "w <- w[order(w$date), ]\n",
        "w <- w[complete.cases(w), ]\n",
        "factors <- names(w)[-1]\n",
        "\n",
        "# check the date range and number of months\n",
        "range(w$date)\n",
        "nrow(w)"
      ],
