    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 7. Compare the Models"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "y6NVUkyigewc"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Now we compare all three models against the benchmark. Accuracy treats every month the same, but an investor cares more about avoiding large losses than about predicting small moves correctly. So we also test a simple **timing strategy**: hold momentum only in months when the model predicts \"Up\", and hold cash otherwise. We compare this strategy's annualized return, Sharpe ratio, and maximum drawdown with always holding momentum."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MurnxKcighAC"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# calculate the annualized Sharpe ratio\n",
        "sharpe <- function(r) mean(r) / sd(r) * sqrt(12)\n",
        "\n",
        "# calculate the maximum drawdown (largest drop from a previous peak)\n",
        "max_dd <- function(r) { g <- cumprod(1 + r); min(g / cummax(g) - 1) }\n",
        "\n",
        "# store the actual momentum returns and predicted probabilities for the testing data\n",
        "r <- df$mom_next[test]\n",
        "posts <- list(LDA = lda.post, QDA = qda.post, NaiveBayes = nb.post)\n",
        "\n",
        "# calculate the performance of always holding momentum\n",
        "hold <- data.frame(model = \"Always hold (always predict Up)\",\n",
        "  accuracy_pct = round(100 * mean(y == \"Up\"), 1),\n",
        "  pct_months_invested = 100,\n",
        "  ann_return_pct = round(100 * mean(r) * 12, 1),\n",
        "  sharpe = round(sharpe(r), 2),\n",
        "  max_drawdown_pct = round(100 * max_dd(r), 1))\n",
        "\n",
        "# calculate the performance of each model's timing strategy\n",
        "timed <- do.call(rbind, lapply(names(posts), function(m) {\n",
        "  p <- posts[[m]]\n",
        "  s <- ifelse(p > 0.5, r, 0)\n",
        "  data.frame(model = m,\n",
        "    accuracy_pct = round(100 * mean((p > 0.5) == (y == \"Up\")), 1),\n",
        "    pct_months_invested = round(100 * mean(p > 0.5), 1),\n",
        "    ann_return_pct = round(100 * mean(s) * 12, 1),\n",
        "    sharpe = round(sharpe(s), 2),\n",
        "    max_drawdown_pct = round(100 * max_dd(s), 1))}))\n",
        "\n",
        "# display the performance comparison for all models\n",
        "results <- rbind(hold, timed)\n",
        "results"
      ],
