    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 8. ROC Curve and AUC\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "lq3fm8-0g1OD"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, we use ROC curves to evaluate how well each model's predicted probabilities separate up months from down months, regardless of the 0.5 cutoff. The AUC summarizes this, where 0.5 means no better than random chance and 1.0 means perfect separation. We also calculate a 95% confidence interval for each AUC."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "B0lrHEvfg5lQ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# create ROC curves using each model's predicted probability of an Up month\n",
        "lda_roc <- roc(y, lda.post, direction = \"<\", levels = c(\"Down\", \"Up\"))\n",
        "qda_roc <- roc(y, qda.post, direction = \"<\", levels = c(\"Down\", \"Up\"))\n",
        "nb_roc <- roc(y, nb.post, direction = \"<\", levels = c(\"Down\", \"Up\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "# plot the three ROC curves\n",
        "plot(lda_roc, col = \"steelblue\", main = \"ROC: Do the Models Rank Up-Months Above Down-Months?\")\n",
        "lines(qda_roc, col = \"lightgrey\")\n",
        "lines(nb_roc, col = \"navy\")\n",
        "legend(\"bottomright\", bty = \"n\", lwd = 2, col = c(\"steelblue\", \"lightgrey\", \"navy\"),\n",
        "       legend = c(\"LDA\", \"QDA\", \"Naive Bayes\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "# calculate the AUC and its 95% confidence interval for each model\n",
        "data.frame(model = c(\"LDA\", \"QDA\", \"Naive Bayes\"),\n",
        "           auc = round(c(auc(lda_roc), auc(qda_roc), auc(nb_roc)), 3),\n",
        "           ci_lower = round(c(ci.auc(lda_roc)[1], ci.auc(qda_roc)[1], ci.auc(nb_roc)[1]), 3),\n",
        "           ci_upper = round(c(ci.auc(lda_roc)[3], ci.auc(qda_roc)[3], ci.auc(nb_roc)[3]), 3))"
      ],
